From 4d7aec855d241730177837ea7be4d9abb9439cb8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:24:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] android: full resolution stills in a separate configuration

With a software ISP the preview and video run in the sensor's binned
mode: the full resolution one costs four times the debayering, and a
1:1 crop of it for a larger stream narrows the field of view. Still
photos were derived from the preview stream, at its resolution.

- A camera may set max_stream_size in the HAL configuration file: YUV
  and implementation defined streams stay within it, and the full
  resolution sizes the camera accepts as they are (4:3 and 16:9) are
  offered as JPEG only, with a one second frame duration.
- A request for such a JPEG is captured in a separate configuration:
  the preview requests in flight complete, the camera switches to the
  full resolution mode, captures one frame (again if it is lost, up to
  three times), and switches back while the JPEG is encoded. The
  other buffers of the request are returned in error. The IPA keeps
  its state across the switch and the lens holds its position.
- Not with a video encoder stream: the switch would freeze the
  recording, and the JPEG stays derived from the largest stream.

---
